### PRIORITY 5: Respiratory Disease Prevention and Early Intervention (COPD, Asthma, RSV, Influenza)

**Definition:** Integrated approach to respiratory disease encompassing vaccination programmes (influenza, COVID, RSV, pneumococcal), early diagnosis and management of COPD and asthma, and pulmonary rehabilitation to reduce winter respiratory admissions.

| Criterion | Score | Rationale |
|-----------|-------|-----------|
| Magnitude of winter problem | 5 | Respiratory disease is the single largest driver of winter emergency admissions in England. COPD alone accounts for ~100,000 emergency admissions annually. Influenza/RSV seasonal surges directly drive winter pressure. |
| Strength of evidence | 5 | Flu vaccination evidence: Cochrane systematic reviews (Jefferson et al., multiple years) — strong evidence for reducing hospitalisation in at-risk groups. COPD management guidelines: GOLD strategy (strong evidence). Pulmonary rehabilitation: NICE CG101 (strong evidence). RSV vaccination: Strong immunogenicity data for older adults (Papi et al., NEJM 2023 for mRNA RSV; Scott et al., NEJM 2023 for RSVPreF). |
| Cost-effectiveness | 5 | Flu vaccination: Highly cost-effective (NICE evidence). Pulmonary rehabilitation: Cost-effective per NICE (Griffiths et al., Lancet 2000 remains foundational; updated evidence available). COPD management: Strong cost-effectiveness evidence. |
| NHS Plan alignment | 5 | Core to NHS Long Term Plan respiratory ambitions. NHSE COPD transformation programme. National flu vaccination programme. JCVI RSV recommendations (2024). |
| Short/medium/long-term impact | 5 | Short-term: Vaccination programmes immediately impactful. Pulmonary rehab: Medium-term capacity building needed. COPD early diagnosis: Medium-long term. |
| Health inequalities reduction | 4 | Respiratory disease disproportionately affects deprived communities. However, vaccination uptake gaps in ethnic minorities and deprived areas remain a challenge requiring active intervention. |
| **Composite Score** | **89/100** | **Very High priority** |

