#### Intervention 4.1: NHS Diabetes Prevention Programme (NDPP) Expansion with Culturally Tailored Approaches

**Implementation Level:** Policy + Clinical

**Mechanism:** NDPP delivers structured behaviour change programme (dietary advice, physical activity, psychological support) to people with non-diabetic hyperglycaemia (pre-diabetes), reducing T2D progression by ~40-50%; prevention of T2D prevents downstream complications that drive emergency admissions

**Resources Required:**
- **Medium:** Programme delivery (face-to-face and digital options); health coach/educator workforce; GP referral system; digital platform for remote delivery

**Implementation Requirements:**
- GP/HbA1c identification and referral system
- Culturally appropriate programme variants (South Asian, Black African/Caribbean)
- Digital delivery option (NHS online programme) for access
- NHS Long Term Plan target: 200,000 places/year

**Strength of Evidence:** **STRONG**
- Diabetes Prevention Program Research Group (DPP). Reduction in the Incidence of Type 2 Diabetes with Lifestyle Intervention or Metformin. N Engl J Med. 2002;346(6):393–403. [Confident — landmark RCT]
- Khunti K, et al. Effectiveness of the NHS Diabetes Prevention Programme in England (NHS DPP evaluation). Lancet Diabetes Endocrinol. 2021;9(11):700–710. [Moderately confident — verify details carefully; UK-specific evaluation]
- NICE PH35 (Type 2 diabetes: prevention in people at high risk, 2012, updated): Evidence base for structured prevention programme

**Feasibility:** **Within 1-3 years** — programme already running; scale-up and equity targeting within this timeframe

**Barriers:**
- Referral pathway completion rates — many high-risk patients not referred
- Completion rates variable (dropout significant, particularly in deprived groups)
- Cultural appropriateness of standard programme

**Metrics:**
- NDPP referral and completion rates by ethnicity and deprivation
- HbA1c change at programme completion
- T2D incidence in NDPP completers vs. eligible non-participants
- Emergency admissions for T2D complications (diabetic foot, DKA, HHS)

**Evidence Category: Strong evidence**

