#### Intervention 10.3: Deprescribing Programmes Targeting Specific High-Risk Drug Classes in Frail Older Adults

**Implementation Level:** Clinical

**Mechanism:** Systematic deprescribing of high-risk drug classes in frail older patients (anticholinergics, benzodiazepines, high-dose NSAIDs, proton pump inhibitors) reduces polypharmacy-related adverse events including falls, confusion, and gastrointestinal bleeding — common causes of emergency admissions in winter

